      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1jdw8zw'
    '|a||Income slides the line; a price tilts it, because the slope is one price divided by the other.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:vxfadw'
    '|a||A straight line assumes a dollar is a dollar, whatever you spend it on. Some budgets break that on purpose.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6560
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Like America''s SNAP, the old food stamps. About forty-two million people get money that can only buy food.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:pio4fs'
    '|a||Say a family has seven hundred dollars in cash and three hundred in SNAP a month. A thousand in cash would give this straight line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ty4s1n'
    '|b||With SNAP, the top is cut flat: food money can''t pay the rent, so at most seven hundred goes on other things.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:15sn5aw'
    '|a||But this family spends more than three hundred on food anyway. For them the missing corner doesn''t matter: SNAP is as good as cash.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1yynxlx'
    '|b||So theory predicts they spend an extra SNAP dollar like an extra cash dollar, and typical estimates say about ten cents of that goes on food.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:16o6fqu'
    '|b||Out of $100 more SNAP, how many dollars went on extra food? Click the line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1kzgmrm'
    '|a||Justine Hastings and Jesse Shapiro followed shoppers'' receipts. Of each extra SNAP dollar, fifty to sixty cents went on food.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Even in families where SNAP was just like cash. They seem to keep food money in its own mental envelope.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ltqj42'
    '|a||Yet when food stamps first rolled out, in the 1960s and 70s, Hilary Hoynes and Diane Schanzenbach found families spent them much like cash.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:d9fx6v'
    '|b||So how sure are we? That the budget line is the edge of what you can buy: consensus. That people treat every dollar alike: contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1q9cysg'
    '|a||Your income doubles, and so does every price. What happens to your budget line?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:pi61hm'
    '|a||It doesn''t move: each end is income over a price, and both double.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5320
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||A sales tax raises every price by 25%; your pay stays the same. What does your budget line do?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Slides inward: both ends shrink by a fifth, and one price over the other is unchanged.':
