      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||A family would spend about $100 a month on childcare, even with more money. They get a $300 voucher that only pays for childcare. On the budget line alone, how does it compare with $300 in cash?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13480
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Worth less: the voucher forces at least $300 onto childcare, so they''re stuck on the cut corner that cash would let them leave.':
